pr_body:
This PR fixes #6669 

The logic for getting the offset for sampling is:
```c++
	auto sample = sample_size;
	if (sample > rows) {
		sample = rows;
	}
	return rows / sample;
```

This let's us scan `sample_size` columns from the dataset.

A problem with this is that if there are null values recurring in the dataset at this offset, the analyzer would only find nulls and set the type as NULL, when a non-null value is encountered it's cast to the result type NULL and that causes this issue.

To combat this issue we now find the first non-null value starting from that the offset, instead of just taking the first value we find at that offset.

comments:
I did a little testing, and it seems to occur whenever your dataset is a multiple of pandas_analyze_sample.

For example, with pandas_analyze_sample = 1000, the error occurs when "n" = 1000, 2000, 3000. And, when pandas_analyze_sample = 999, the error occurs when n = 999, 999*2, etc

Without looking at the sampling code, my guess is when the data repetition is aligned with pandas_analyze_sample, duckdb is always sampling the same element N times.

This is surprising to me, as I had assumed that pandas_analyze_sample was actually reading the first N items... not actually sampling. 

---
Edit: 

I think this explains it: 
```
uint64_t PandasAnalyzer::GetSampleIncrement(idx_t rows) {
	D_ASSERT(sample_size != 0);
	//! Apply the maximum
	auto sample = sample_size;
	if (sample > rows) {
		sample = rows;
	}
	return rows / sample;
}
```
https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/blob/79f67b86260c76cd54175b9dd91d7924761a9f44/tools/pythonpkg/src/pandas_analyzer.cpp#L336]

If you have 3201 * 1000 rows, with pandas_analyze_sample = 1000, then it'll increment every 3201 rows... in other words: it's sampling the same element repeatedly.
